{"products":{"guppy":[{"id":"g1","name":"JET BLACK","price":180,"unit":"pair","desc":"The Jet Black Guppy is a striking ornamental freshwater fish known for its deep, solid-black coloration.\n\nColor: Rich, jet-black body and fins; high-quality males may appear almost completely black.\n\nBody shape: Small, slender, and laterally compressed, with a graceful flowing tail.\n\nSize: Males usually grow to around 3–4 cm, while females can reach 5–6 cm.\n\nTemperament: Peaceful, active, and generally suitable for community aquariums.\n\nWater: Prefers clean, well-filtered freshwater with stable conditions; moderately hard, slightly alkaline water is often suitable.\n\nDiet: Omnivorous—can be fed quality flakes, micro-pellets, and occasional frozen/live foods.\n\nBreeding: Livebearers. Females give birth to free-swimming fry rather than laying eggs.\n\nLifespan: Typically around 1.5–2.5 years with good care.\n\nBest feature: The contrast between its dark black coloration and bright aquarium plants makes it an excellent centerpiece or schooling fish.","image":"media/1791310258475_WhatsApp_Image_2026_10_06_at_11.07.59_AM.jpg","video":"media/1791310260212_WhatsApp_Video_2026_10_06_at_11.10.38_AM.mp4","out":false},{"id":"g2","name":"Blue Moscow Guppy","price":150,"unit":"pair","image":""},{"id":"g3","name":"Albino Full Red","price":200,"unit":"pair","image":""},{"id":"g4","name":"Black Moscow Guppy","price":150,"unit":"pair","image":""},{"id":"g5","name":"Cobra Guppy","price":120,"unit":"pair","image":""},{"id":"g6","name":"Mosaic Guppy","price":120,"unit":"pair","image":""},{"id":"g7","name":"Yellow Tuxedo Guppy","price":130,"unit":"pair","image":""},{"id":"g8","name":"Snakeskin Guppy","price":130,"unit":"pair","image":""}],"otherfish":[{"id":"o1","name":"Molly","price":60,"unit":"pair","image":""},{"id":"o2","name":"Platy","price":50,"unit":"pair","image":""},{"id":"o3","name":"Swordtail","price":60,"unit":"pair","image":""},{"id":"o4","name":"Betta","price":150,"unit":"piec